2026-05-23T00:00Z claude created — pattern found during quickfixes session celebrate sweep

--- body ---
## Context

The `scripts/check-agnostic.sh` check runs on `tickets/` as well as `skills/`.
During the quickfixes session (2026-05-23), tickets 0166 and 0171 were committed
to main with `/home/haduong/<repo>/<file>` examples in their bodies — authored
by the HDMX-coding-agent with actual session paths. The agnostic-guard caught it
only at CI time on the first PR (t170), requiring a fixup commit before merge.

The root cause is agents writing ticket bodies with real paths from their session
context instead of `~/<repo>/<file>` or `$HOME/<repo>/<file>`.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] A pre-commit hook or `make check` target runs `check-agnostic.sh tickets/`
      and fails if any open ticket body contains a `/home/[a-z]` pattern.
- [ ] The check runs on `tickets/` only (closed tickets in `tickets/closed/`
      are already frozen — no need to amend them).
- [ ] At least one adherence test in `tests/` exercises the check against a
      synthetic ticket body containing a hardcoded home path and asserts failure.
- [ ] `make check` passes after the change.

## Notes

- This is a class-shape regression guard: the same anti-pattern can recur any
  time an agent creates a ticket from within a session with real paths.
- Keep the fix minimal: the check already exists; this is just about running it
  automatically on commit or in the test suite, not rewriting the check.
